text:
nina_sales: FYI incoming POC: large payments processor. Requirements: streaming generation + function calls that emit NDJSON (newline-delimited JSON) lines, strict JSON schema versioning, SSO (OIDC preferred), customer-managed KMS, and procurement wants a pilot price. Can eng/sec/ops confirm feasibility and quick checklist? :eyes:

omar_eng: Quick clarifiers: 1) Do they require strict schema version enforcement server-side or will client-side validation suffice? 2) Are function calls sync (inline) or long-running async jobs? 3) Target p99 latency and qps?

nina_sales: They want server-side schema version tags (we should stamp v1/v2 on outputs). Mostly inline function calls for real-time risk checks; occasional async for batch enrichment. Target: 60 qps peak, p99 < 300ms for inline.

omar_eng: Notes: server-side stamping we can add as metadata in each function_call event (e.g., "schema_version":"v1"). For streaming NDJSON best pattern is SSE with explicit event types: response_chunk, function_call, function_result. Client reads line-by-line and validates JSON per schema_version. Example pseudocode (JS):
```js
const es = new EventSource(url)
es.onmessage = (e) => {
  const obj = JSON.parse(e.data)
  if (obj.type === 'function_call') {
    // obj.payload.arguments -> validate against schema v1
  }
}
```

tess_sec: Security items: OIDC OK. For CMK we support AWS KMS / GCP KMS on Dedicated and Private. Hosted CMK needs contract addendum. We'll require SCIM + IP allowlist for the admin console and recommend short-lived API tokens for apps. If they need FIPS/HSM, that moves to enterprise engineering and will add lead time.

liam_ops: Ops/ordering: To guarantee per-conversation ordering use Dedicated with session pinning to a connection id. SSE over HTTP/2 is fine but if they want bi-directional low-latency control, websocket is better. For NDJSON ingestion, ensure backpressure handling on their side (we stream line-by-line). We'll enable token-level breakdown and trace export to their SIEM.

nina_sales: Procurement pricing please for pilot: 1 month, 60 qps sustained, ~200k tokens/day streaming + function calls. Any ballpark hosted vs dedicated?

omar_eng: Ballpark hosted: streaming ~ $0.00075/token example for rtb models. 200k/day * 30 = 6M tokens -> ~$4.5k/mo. If they need ordering SLA and guaranteed pinned throughput pick Dedicated: expect reserved commit starting ~$20k/month for a modest pool. We can suggest hybrid: start hosted dev, reserved tier for pilots with ordering SLA.

tess_sec: Security review timeline: standard questionnaire + OIDC + KMS integration ~2 weeks. If we need mTLS for webhooks or on-prem HSM add another 1-2 weeks. SCIM provisioning adds a few days for testing.

liam_ops: I'll queue a Dedicated sizing job if they sign. Also suggestion: include a cheaper INT8-quantized fallback model for cost-sensitive spikes; we can auto-failover at 95th percentile.

nina_sales: Great. Can we get a short customer-facing integration checklist and a tiny sample NDJSON line schema? I'll attach to the SAQ reply.

omar_eng: Checklist (compact): 1) Confirm model + token budget 2) Choose hosting mode (Hosted / Dedicated / Private) 3) SSO type (OIDC/SAML) + SCIM 4) KMS choice (AWS/GCP/Redwood) 5) Decide sync vs async function flows & webhook mTLS 6) Provide JSON schema(s) + versioning rules 7) Telemetry/SIEM endpoint + retention 8) Pilot dates + success criteria

omar_eng: Sample NDJSON line (one line per record):
{"event":"function_call","schema_version":"v1","function":"risk_score","arguments":{"tx_id":"abc123","amount":123.45}}

deploy-bot: [task] queued Dedicated sizing job id ds-7782. No action required unless overrides supplied.

liam_ops: I'll prepare SIEM export docs and a recommended backpressure pattern for NDJSON ingestion. Also will prepare a short fallback policy for quantized models.

nina_sales: Perfect. I'll send this with the SAQ and request NDA to share architecture diagram for Private. Thanks all! :pray:
